# Controlled agentic development

- Read the relevant implementation and nearest `AGENTS.md` before editing.
- Treat code, tests, schemas, and configuration as the source of truth.
- For non-trivial work, define current behavior, desired behavior, constraints, acceptance criteria, and contract participants before implementation.
- Make the smallest coherent change. Do not refactor, rename, reformat, or upgrade unrelated code.
- Do not stop merely because a correct cross-layer change requires several files; explain why every touched file is necessary.
- Debug with reproduction, hypotheses, evidence, root cause, targeted fix, and regression coverage.
- Review generated changes as untrusted code before finishing.
- Run relevant verification and distinguish passed checks from unverified behavior.
- Never claim a command, test, build, camera check, or Firebase check succeeded unless it was actually executed and observed.
- Do not deploy, publish, mutate production data, or add secrets without an explicit user request.
- Finish substantial tasks with behavior changed, files changed, commands/results, assumptions, risks, and `Not verified` items.
